cd552ad5 (727 1793276020987 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f382") (src . "edit tools: one lexical fold finds the edit directory's sidecar\n\nedit-export, edit-sync and landing-freeze --tree each built the edit\ndirectory's sidecar as the spelling given plus \".edit\", so a directory\nnamed as \".\", \"./\", \"dir/.\" or \"dir/sub/..\" gave a path such as\n<cwd>/..edit: edit-sync refused missing-sidecar for a valid directory,\nand edit-export of `new/.` put its sidecar inside the new directory. All\nthree now fold the spelling first, with one shared function: made\nabsolute from the current directory, empty and \".\" components dropped,\n\"..\" removing the component before it (at the root it stays). It is\nlexical: nothing on disk is asked and no link is resolved, so a\ndirectory named through a link keeps its sidecar beside the link, as\nedit-export wrote it, and \"lnk/..\" is the link's parent, as the shell's\nlogical cd .. is. landing-freeze no longer refuses a final \".\" or \"..\";\na bare --tree is still a usage error. The store path is not folded.\n\n- landing-files.sc: edit-dir-path, the fold.\n- tools/edit-export.sc, tools/edit-sync.sc, tools/landing-freeze.sc: the\n  directory folded before \".edit\" is appended.\n- README: the edit tools' paragraph says so.\n- Tests: edit-tools (an export through \"..\", syncs and freezes spelled\n  \".\", \"./\", \"dir/.\", \"dir/x/..\", a link-named directory, the link's\n  parent); rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 511))))
