96d57bdd (745 1793277645612 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f378") (src . "supply reads .gitignore before its lock; --clear writes nothing it need not\n\nsupply refused a .gitignore of the wrong kind before taking its table\nlock, but read it inside the lock, which first makes derived/ and its lock\nfile, so a .gitignore that could not be read refused after both existed.\nIt is now read and merged before the lock, and inside it only the bytes\nalready computed are written, or nothing. supply --clear took the table\nlock whatever was there, so on a store with no derived/ it made the\ndirectory and its lock to remove a table that could not exist. It now\nlooks once: with no derived/ it writes nothing and answers as before; a\ndirectory is locked and the table removed as before; anything else is\nrefused derived-not-a-directory before any write. --clear writes no\n.gitignore, so it is not gated on one. The comment and the README state\nthe remaining window between looking and writing.\n\n- derived.sc: ignored-bytes before the lock; clear-derived's one look.\n- README: the supply section says so.\n- Tests: supply (an unreadable .gitignore makes nothing, a --clear with no\n  derived/ makes nothing, a linked .gitignore does not stop --clear, a\n  derived that is a file is refused); unreadable-census; rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 512))))
